Not covered by this licence, and not distributed with this repository:

- No ROM images. The program runs on the Commodore 64's own KERNAL and
  BASIC ROMs (it calls the BASIC ROM's floating-point routines), so it
  needs a real C64 or an emulator that brings the original ROMs. VICE's
  installation provides them (tools/install_vice_roms.sh fetches the five
  the tests need from the VICE source release into ~/.local/share/vice;
  they are never copied into the repository).
- No emulator. VICE is a separate GPL program the tests and the media
  scripts run; nothing of it is included.
- The screen images in docs/img/c64/ are screenshots of this program
  running in VICE: the C64 character set and colours in them are the
  emulator's rendering of the C64 ROMs and video chip.
